{"availability":"available","full":"ashutosh887/cleargate","name":"cleargate","description":"A bank voice support agent you'd actually trust: it can refund money, but every tool call goes through AgntID. ClearGate, the go-live gate, attacks it, proposes policy, gates CI and signs the proof. Works for any agent.","category":"Finance","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-10T06:18:55Z","updated":"2026-10-10T10:26:13Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://trycleargate.vercel.app","topics":["agent-security","agntid","ai-agents","ai-governance","authorization","devops","fintech","github-actions","llm-security","mcp","owasp","red-teaming","voice-ai"],"demo":"https://trycleargate.vercel.app/try","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:48.064Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:48.064Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:48.064Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T11:06:48.064Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The agent acts. AgntID decides. The engineer signs.","We built a voice support agent for a bank's failed-payment line. It takes calls in Hindi and English and works as a team: voice → accounts → payments → ops. It can refund real money, so it acts only through AgntID, which decides every tool call it makes. ClearGate is the go-live gate that proves it: it attacks the gated agent beside the same agent with no guardrails, evolves the attacks, proposes the AgntID policy, gates CI and signs a record anyone can verify offline.","Where it stands. Everything is built, and every number here was measured on the local stand-in of AgntID's decisions, labelled \"not AgntID\" in each record. The AgntID runtime is set up on our machine. No live run has completed yet; scripts/liveall.sh runs them and fills the live table."],"features":["Place a call in your browser:"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ashutosh887/cleargate/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint"